"Chinese_zodiac": {"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Tang_Pottery_Zodiac_Figures_%289948253544%29.jpg/1920px-Tang_Pottery_Zodiac_Figures_%289948253544%29.jpg","title":"Pottery figures of the twelve animals","desc":"A row of Tang pottery figures with human bodies and animal heads, which the file's own record identifies as zodiac figures in the Shaanxi Provincial Museum, Xi'an. CC0, via Wikimedia Commons.","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tang_Pottery_Zodiac_Figures_(9948253544).jpg","alt":"Four standing pottery figures in a museum case, each with a human body in a long belted robe and its hands folded inside its sleeves, and each with the head of an animal: from the left a rodent, a horned ox, a broad-faced cat and a long-eared hare, all of them looking upward and standing on ringed plinths."},
"Chiyou": {"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/%E5%B1%B1%E4%B8%9C%E7%9C%81%E6%B2%82%E5%8D%97%E5%8E%BF_%E6%B1%89%E7%94%BB%E5%83%8F%E7%9F%B3_%E8%9A%A9%E5%B0%A4%E4%BA%94%E5%85%B5.jpg/960px-%E5%B1%B1%E4%B8%9C%E7%9C%81%E6%B2%82%E5%8D%97%E5%8E%BF_%E6%B1%89%E7%94%BB%E5%83%8F%E7%9F%B3_%E8%9A%A9%E5%B0%A4%E4%BA%94%E5%85%B5.jpg","title":"Chiyou and the five weapons","desc":"Rubbing of a Han pictorial stone from Yinan, Shandong, showing Chiyou with the five weapons: a bow and arrows above his head, blades in both hands and swords sprouting from his limbs. Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons.","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%B1%B1%E4%B8%9C%E7%9C%81%E6%B2%82%E5%8D%97%E5%8E%BF_%E6%B1%89%E7%94%BB%E5%83%8F%E7%9F%B3_%E8%9A%A9%E5%B0%A4%E4%BA%94%E5%85%B5.jpg","alt":"Rubbing of a Han stone relief: a squat beast-faced figure with a bow and arrows above his head and blades sprouting from his arms and legs"},
