"Oscan": {"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/OsqueBritishMuseum.jpg/1920px-OsqueBritishMuseum.jpg","title":"Oscan","desc":"Stele bearing an inscription in Oscan (British Museum, London). Around 300 - 100 BCE.C. Found in the inner arch of the Nola Gate in Pompeii. Reads from right to left: \"Vibius Popidius, son of Vibius, chief magistrate, was responsible for this work and approved it\". Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons.","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:OsqueBritishMuseum.jpg","alt":"OsqueBritishMuseum"},
"Ostracism": {"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Athen_Stoa_Ostrakismos_2.jpg/1920px-Athen_Stoa_Ostrakismos_2.jpg","title":"Ostracism","alt":"Twelve broken pot bases mounted in rows on a museum wall, each with a Greek name scratched around the ring through the black glaze","desc":"These ostraka from 482 BCE were recovered from a well near the Acropolis. The ostraca in the upper row read 'THEMISTHOKLES PHREARIOS', while the others read 'THEMISTHOKLES NEOKLEOS'. Xocolatl, public domain, via Wikimedia Commons.","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Athen_Stoa_Ostrakismos_2.jpg"},
"Out_of_Africa_I": {"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/ISS035-E-007148_Nile_-_Sinai_-_Dead_Sea_-_Wide_Angle_View.jpg/1280px-ISS035-E-007148_Nile_-_Sinai_-_Dead_Sea_-_Wide_Angle_View.jpg","title":"Out of Africa I","desc":"The meeting point of Africa and Asia seen from orbit: the Nile valley, the Sinai Peninsula between two arms of the Red Sea, and the coast of the Levant beyond.","credit":"Expedition 35 Crew, NASA Johnson Space Center, processed by Julian Herzog, Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons. https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ISS035-E-007148_Nile_-_Sinai_-_Dead_Sea_-_Wide_Angle_View.jpg","alt":"A photograph taken from space over north-east Africa, showing pale desert crossed by the dark green ribbon of the Nile and its delta on the left, the deep blue Red Sea splitting into two narrow gulfs around the triangular Sinai Peninsula in the centre, the Mediterranean Sea above, and brown and reddish uplands of Arabia and the Levant to the right under the curve of the horizon."},
"Pacific_Northwest_Coast": {"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Ceremonial_cape%2C_Tlingit_people%2C_Chilkat_clan%2C_northwest_coast_of_North_America%2C_1850-1900_AD%2C_cedar_bark%2C_mountain_goat_hair%2C_sheep%27s_wool%2C_view_1_-_Textile_Museum%2C_George_Washington_University_-_DSC09926.JPG/1920px-thumbnail.jpg","title":"Pacific Northwest Coast","desc":"Exhibit in the Textile Museum, George Washington University, Washington, DC, USA. Photography was permitted in the museum without restriction. This work is old enough so that it is in the public domain. Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons.","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ceremonial_cape,_Tlingit_people,_Chilkat_clan,_northwest_coast_of_North_America,_1850-1900_AD,_cedar_bark,_mountain_goat_hair,_sheep%27s_wool,_view_1_-_Textile_Museum,_George_Washington_University_-_DSC09926.JPG","alt":"Ceremonial cape, Tlingit people, Chilkat clan, northwest coast of North America, 1850-1900 CE, cedar bark, mountain goat hair, sheep's wool, view 1 - Textile Museum, George Washington University"},
