"Spartan_mirage": {"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Ancient_Sparta_ruins_%281%29.jpg/1920px-Ancient_Sparta_ruins_%281%29.jpg","title":"Spartan mirage","alt":"Low stone footings among grass and trees on the site of ancient Sparta","desc":"Ruins on the site of ancient Sparta, the low remains Thucydides had in mind when he wrote that a deserted Lacedaemon would leave posterity refusing to believe her fame matched her power. Peulle, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ancient_Sparta_ruins_(1).jpg"},
"Spartan_women": {"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Spartan_running_girl_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Spartan_running_girl_%28cropped%29.jpg","title":"Spartan women","desc":"Bronze figure of a running girl, 520–500 BCE, Spartan, found at Prizren. The short chiton baring one breast matches the outfit Pausanias says was worn by athletes competing in the Heraean Games. British Museum 1876,0510.1. Caeciliusinhorto, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Spartan_running_girl_(cropped).jpg","alt":"A bronze figure of a girl in mid-stride, wearing a short chiton that bares one breast, mounted on a museum stand"},
