"Capitoline_Wolf": {"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Sex._Pompeius%2C_AR_denarius%2C_137_BC%2C_RRC_235-1c.jpg/1920px-Sex._Pompeius%2C_AR_denarius%2C_137_BC%2C_RRC_235-1c.jpg","title":"Capitoline Wolf","desc":"A Roman silver denarius of 137 BCE, its reverse showing the she-wolf suckling the twins with the shepherd Faustulus beside them","credit":"Classical Numismatic Group, CC BY-SA 2.5, via Wikimedia Commons. https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sex._Pompeius%2C_AR_denarius%2C_137_BC%2C_RRC_235-1c.jpg","alt":"Two faces of a worn silver coin, the left a helmeted head of Roma, the right a she-wolf suckling two infants with a standing figure at the side and a fig tree behind"},
