"Hellenistic_kingship": {"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Syria_-_king_Antiochos_II_-_261-246_BC_-_silver_tetradrachm_-_head_of_Antiochos_I_-_Apollon_-_Berlin_MK_AM_18203078.jpg/1280px-Syria_-_king_Antiochos_II_-_261-246_BC_-_silver_tetradrachm_-_head_of_Antiochos_I_-_Apollon_-_Berlin_MK_AM_18203078.jpg","title":"A Seleucid king in the diadem","desc":"A silver tetradrachm struck at Seleucia on the Tigris; the plain band tied round the head is the diadem, the one mark that said its wearer was a king.","credit":"Photograph by ArchaiOptix, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons. https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Syria_-_king_Antiochos_II_-_261-246_BC_-_silver_tetradrachm_-_head_of_Antiochos_I_-_Apollon_-_Berlin_MK_AM_18203078.jpg","alt":"A worn silver coin showing a man's head in profile with a narrow band tied round the hair, its ends falling behind the neck."},
